From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:14:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: apple,scaler: let the T8132 engine name
 its reset

The J604 runtime ADT gives /arm-io/scaler0 a function-device_reset that
points at PMGR state 0x99, the MSR power state at PMGR +0x560 (ps_msr),
and the driver pulses an optional reset before its first job. The T8132
branch of the binding lists no resets property, so a node carrying it
fails validation through unevaluatedProperties. Allow one reset there, as
the T6041 and T8140 branches already do (they require it).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,scaler.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,scaler.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,scaler.yaml
index e7e0413371..9a89c50d1e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,scaler.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,scaler.yaml
@@ -74,6 +74,9 @@ allOf:
         clocks:
           maxItems: 1
 
+        resets:
+          maxItems: 1
+
       required:
         - compatible
         - reg
